# =============================================================================
# FAULTMAVEN — STANDALONE CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================
# Quick start:
#   1. cp .env.example .env
#   2. Pick ONE LLM provider below and set its API key
#   3. ./faultmaven start    →    http://localhost:3333
#
# This file configures the STANDALONE deployment ONLY — a single-process,
# single-user FaultMaven on one machine (SQLite, in-process cache, embedded
# ChromaDB, local files, local auth). Those backends are fixed defaults, so the
# surface you actually set is tiny: an LLM provider + key, and a couple of
# optional toggles. Everything omitted here has a safe code default.
#
# CLOUD is NOT configured here. The cloud deployment (multi-user, Postgres,
# Redis, OAuth, multi-tenancy, observability) is configured via Kubernetes
# ConfigMaps/Secrets — see ADR-004 (config-surface split) and ADR-006
# (multi-tenancy is a cloud-only capability). FaultMaven Cloud subscribers don't
# need this file at all — point the extension at https://app.faultmaven.ai
#
# Running standalone on a remote box? Keep the config as localhost and tunnel:
#   ssh -L 3333:localhost:3333 -L 8090:localhost:8090 user@server
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. LLM PROVIDER  (REQUIRED — the one thing you must set)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE provider, then set its API key below (optionally pin a model).

# CHAT_PROVIDER=anthropic
# CHAT_PROVIDER=openai
# CHAT_PROVIDER=gemini
# CHAT_PROVIDER=fireworks
# CHAT_PROVIDER=groq
# CHAT_PROVIDER=huggingface
# CHAT_PROVIDER=cohere
# CHAT_PROVIDER=openrouter
# CHAT_PROVIDER=local              # Ollama / vLLM — fully offline, no API key

# --- Credentials: set the key (and optionally the model) for your provider ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxx
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-xxx
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# GEMINI_API_KEY=xxx
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=fw-xxx
# FIREWORKS_MODEL=accounts/fireworks/models/qwen2.5-coder-32b-instruct
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk-xxx
# GROQ_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=hf_xxx
# HUGGINGFACE_MODEL=mistralai/Mistral-Large-Instruct-2411
# COHERE_API_KEY=xxx
# COHERE_CHAT_MODEL=command-r-plus
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-xxx
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet
# Local LLM (Ollama/vLLM):
# LOCAL_LLM_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434   # Linux: http://172.17.0.1:11434
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=llama3.2

# After first start you manage these in the Dashboard (read-only status in
# standalone — .env stays the source of truth; edit here and restart to change).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPTIONAL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web search (requires a Tavily key):
# ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH=true
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-xxx

# Log level: DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR (default: INFO)
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. AUTH  (standalone = single-user local auth)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standalone always uses local auth (one owner, username login). OAuth/multi-user
# is a cloud capability; AUTH_MODE stays 'local' here.
#
# Secret that signs your local session tokens. CHANGE THIS to a long random
# string before exposing the server beyond your own machine.
JWT_SECRET_KEY=dev-secret-change-me

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. CONTAINER IMAGES  (advanced — only relevant to ./faultmaven.sh)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ./faultmaven.sh start pulls PRE-BUILT images from the GitHub Container Registry
# (ghcr.io/faultmaven/faultmaven and …/faultmaven-dashboard). Both tags default
# to :latest. Pin them for a reproducible, version-matched stack — use a release
# version (e.g. 1.0.0) or an immutable per-build tag (sha-<short-sha>):
# FM_IMAGE_TAG=latest
# FM_DASHBOARD_IMAGE_TAG=latest
#
# To run your own source instead of these images, leave the tags unset and build
# from source: `./faultmaven.sh start --build` (API) / `--build-dashboard` (UI).

# =============================================================================
# Notes
# =============================================================================
# • Fixed standalone backends (not set here): SQLite, in-process cache, embedded
#   ChromaDB, local file storage, local auth. Postgres/Redis/S3/multi-tenancy are
#   cloud-only and configured via Kubernetes, never in this file.
# • DEPLOYMENT_MODE defaults to 'standalone' — do NOT set 'cloud' here. Cloud is
#   driven by Kubernetes config, and the server fails fast on boot if it is told
#   'cloud' without the required cloud infrastructure (ADR-004 coherence gate).
